From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:43:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 113/117] iio: light: tsl2583: Describe Apple ALS variants
 through match data

The CT821 support keyed every chip-specific decision off a single boolean.
Apple pairs the same TSL258x register interface with more than one part,
and those parts differ in the gain register, in how the ALS interrupt is
cleared, in the extra control bits they need, and in the layout of their
factory LSCI calibration record.

Move all of that into the per-part match data and rename the shared code
paths accordingly. The calibration parser now takes the record version, the
record size, the gain-step count and the fixed-point scale of the recorded
gain ratios from the match data instead of hard-coding the CT821 v3 record.

No functional change for the existing parts.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
[Orchard: ported to v7.3-rc1: power-on call in mainline's formatting, using the per-part cntl_enable]

Orchard-replay-of: c241a321fefb5b9eebdff7a874f2dab94918b8ce
